    {
      "id": "A04",
      "label": "SQL Server's decimal scale: Quantity x UnitPrice x TaxRate / 100.0 is decimal(38,6), so 0.0049999 becomes 0.004999 before ROUND; NULL UnitPrice and a zero rate",
      "traps": [
        "numeric-rounding"
      ],
      "reasoning": "The product int x decimal(18,2) x decimal(18,3) exceeds precision 38, and the division by 100.0 is cut to scale 6 on SQL Server; PostgreSQL keeps all digits. 0.0049999 and 0.0050001 sit on either side of the 2-place midpoint. UnitPrice NULL gives NULL for every total; TaxRate 0.000 gives a tax of 0.00.",
